```

This test will fail when Contains(x) returns false. The assertion verifies that when Contains(x) returns false, then the last index of x in the original list is less than or equal to the index of x in the new list. 

You typically use a tool such as Pex (Pex for .NET) to automatically generate unit tests using the contracts present in the code. It uses these contracts to generate test inputs and to specify postconditions and invariants. While it may not be the case for this question, you can use Pex to generate additional edge-cases not catered by tests written by hand.--------------------